## Article 42. Parties to the case

```catala
declaration scope Article42Parties:
  input participant content Participant
  output isParty content YesNo
  output hasProceduralRights content YesNo

scope Article42Parties:
  label party_default definition isParty equals No

# Plaintiff and defendant are always parties
  label party_plaintiff exception party_default
  definition isParty under condition
    participant.role = PlaintiffRole
    consequence equals Yes

  label party_defendant exception party_default
  definition isParty under condition
    participant.role = DefendantRole
    consequence equals Yes

# Parties always have procedural rights
  label rights_parties definition hasProceduralRights under condition
    isParty = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label rights_non_parties definition hasProceduralRights under condition
    isParty = No
    consequence equals No
```

## Article 43. Co-participants

```catala
declaration scope Article43CoParticipants:
  input multiplePlaintiffs content YesNo
  input multipleDefendants content YesNo
  input sameLegalBasis content YesNo
  output canJoinAsCoParticipants content YesNo

scope Article43CoParticipants:
  label join_default definition canJoinAsCoParticipants equals No

# Multiple plaintiffs or defendants with same legal basis
  label join_co_plaintiffs exception join_default
  definition canJoinAsCoParticipants under condition
    multiplePlaintiffs = Yes
    and sameLegalBasis = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label join_co_defendants exception join_default
  definition canJoinAsCoParticipants under condition
    multipleDefendants = Yes
    and sameLegalBasis = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 44. Rights of parties

```catala
declaration scope Article44PartyRights:
  input participant content Participant
  output canFamiliarizeWithCaseMaterials content YesNo
  output canMakeExcerpts content YesNo
  output canFileMotions content YesNo
  output canPresentEvidence content YesNo
  output canParticipateInHearing content YesNo
  output canMakeArguments content YesNo
  output canFileAppeals content YesNo
  output canObjectToMotions content YesNo

scope Article44PartyRights:
# All parties have the full set of procedural rights
  label rights_familiarize definition canFamiliarizeWithCaseMaterials equals Yes
  label rights_excerpts definition canMakeExcerpts equals Yes
  label rights_motions definition canFileMotions equals Yes
  label rights_evidence definition canPresentEvidence equals Yes
  label rights_hearing definition canParticipateInHearing equals Yes
  label rights_arguments definition canMakeArguments equals Yes
  label rights_appeals definition canFileAppeals equals Yes
  label rights_object definition canObjectToMotions equals Yes
```

## Article 45. Duties of parties

```catala
declaration scope Article45PartyDuties:
  input participant content Participant
  output mustActInGoodFaith content YesNo
  output mustDiscloseEvidence content YesNo
  output mustNotifyAddressChanges content YesNo
  output mustRespectCourtProcedure content YesNo

scope Article45PartyDuties:
  label duty_good_faith definition mustActInGoodFaith equals Yes
  label duty_disclose definition mustDiscloseEvidence equals Yes
  label duty_notify definition mustNotifyAddressChanges equals Yes
  label duty_respect definition mustRespectCourtProcedure equals Yes
```

## Article 46. Third parties

```catala
declaration scope Article46ThirdParties:
  input participant content Participant
  input independentClaims content YesNo
  input sharesLegalInterest content YesNo
  output canJoinAsThirdParty content YesNo
  output thirdPartyType content ParticipantRole

scope Article46ThirdParties:
  label third_default definition canJoinAsThirdParty equals No

# Third party with independent claims
  label third_independent exception third_default
  definition canJoinAsThirdParty under condition
    independentClaims = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label third_independent_type definition thirdPartyType under condition
    independentClaims = Yes
    consequence equals ThirdPartyClaimant

# Third party without independent claims but sharing legal interest
  label third_shared exception third_default
  definition canJoinAsThirdParty under condition
    independentClaims = No
    and sharesLegalInterest = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label third_shared_type definition thirdPartyType under condition
    independentClaims = No
    and sharesLegalInterest = Yes
    consequence equals ThirdPartyDefendant
```

## Article 47. Interested persons

```catala
declaration scope Article47InterestedPersons:
  input legalInterestAffected content YesNo
  input notPartyToCase content YesNo
  output canParticipateAsInterested content YesNo

scope Article47InterestedPersons:
  label interested_default definition canParticipateAsInterested equals No

  label interested_exception exception interested_default
  definition canParticipateAsInterested under condition
    legalInterestAffected = Yes
    and notPartyToCase = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 48. Prosecutor participation

```catala
declaration scope Article48Prosecutor:
  input prosecutorInitiatesCase content YesNo
  input prosecutorJoinsCase content YesNo
  input prosecutorFilesStatement content YesNo
  output prosecutorHasPartyRights content YesNo
  output prosecutorMustProveGrounds content YesNo

scope Article48Prosecutor:
# Prosecutor who initiates case has plaintiff rights
  label prosecutor_initiator_rights definition prosecutorHasPartyRights under condition
    prosecutorInitiatesCase = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label prosecutor_joiner_rights definition prosecutorHasPartyRights under condition
    prosecutorJoinsCase = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Prosecutor who initiates must prove grounds
  label prosecutor_burden definition prosecutorMustProveGrounds under condition
    prosecutorInitiatesCase = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label prosecutor_no_burden definition prosecutorMustProveGrounds under condition
    prosecutorInitiatesCase = No
    consequence equals No
```

## Article 49. State body intervention

```catala
declaration scope Article49StateBodyIntervention:
  input stateBodyHasCompetence content YesNo
  input disputeInvolvesPublicAuthority content YesNo
  input stateBodyRequestsIntervention content YesNo
  output stateBodyCanIntervene content YesNo

scope Article49StateBodyIntervention:
  label intervene_default definition stateBodyCanIntervene equals No

  label intervene_exception exception intervene_default
  definition stateBodyCanIntervene under condition
    stateBodyHasCompetence = Yes
    and disputeInvolvesPublicAuthority = Yes
    and stateBodyRequestsIntervention = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Articles 50-55. Procedural capacity and representation

```catala
declaration scope Article50ProceduralCapacity:
  input participant content Participant
  output hasFullProceduralCapacity content YesNo
  output needsRepresentative content YesNo

scope Article50ProceduralCapacity:
# Individuals with legal capacity have full procedural capacity
  label capacity_full definition hasFullProceduralCapacity under condition
    participant.isIndividual = Yes
    and participant.hasLegalCapacity = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label capacity_limited definition hasFullProceduralCapacity under condition
    participant.isIndividual = Yes
    and participant.hasLegalCapacity = No
    consequence equals No

  label capacity_entity definition hasFullProceduralCapacity under condition
    participant.isIndividual = No
    consequence equals Yes

# Those without capacity need representatives
  label needs_rep_yes definition needsRepresentative under condition
    hasFullProceduralCapacity = No
    consequence equals Yes

  label needs_rep_no definition needsRepresentative under condition
    hasFullProceduralCapacity = Yes
    consequence equals No

declaration scope Article51Representation:
  input participant content Participant
  output canHaveRepresentative content YesNo
  output representativeTypeAllowed content RepresentativeType

scope Article51Representation:
# Any party can have a representative
  label can_have_rep definition canHaveRepresentative equals Yes

# Representative type based on situation
  label rep_legal definition representativeTypeAllowed under condition
    participant.hasLegalCapacity = No
    consequence equals LegalRepresentative

  label rep_attorney definition representativeTypeAllowed under condition
    participant.hasLegalCapacity = Yes
    consequence equals Attorney

declaration scope Article53ForeignParticipant:
  input participant content Participant
  output hasEqualProceduralRights content YesNo
  output mayNeedDiplomaticRepresentation content YesNo

scope Article53ForeignParticipant:
  label foreign_equal definition hasEqualProceduralRights equals Yes

  label diplomatic_default definition mayNeedDiplomaticRepresentation equals No

  label diplomatic_exception exception diplomatic_default
  definition mayNeedDiplomaticRepresentation under condition
    participant.isForeignParticipant = Yes
    and participant.isIndividual = No
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Articles 56-60. Participant changes and succession

```catala
declaration scope Article56Succession:
  input plaintiffReplaced content YesNo
  input defendantReplaced content YesNo
  input successorConsents content YesNo
  output successionAllowed content YesNo

scope Article56Succession:
  label succession_default definition successionAllowed equals No

# Universal succession (reorganization, death, etc.)
  label succession_plaintiff exception succession_default
  definition successionAllowed under condition
    plaintiffReplaced = Yes
    and successorConsents = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label succession_defendant exception succession_default
  definition successionAllowed under condition
    defendantReplaced = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```
